# Drafted by Gemini (R22 n3), edited.

~ oven_start
set n3_started
Narrator: You step into a brick oven the size of a parlour, where fat drips hissing onto a bed of white-hot coals. On one iron spit turns a plucked turkey with a lizard's tail, and on the other hangs Gilly Jenkin in three heavy chains.
nm_stonoga [smile]: Mind the basting, darlings, or the meat dries right out! My sisters can fuss with heads and hearts, I know a proper feast starts with tender flesh.
quest crooked_nightmare crooked_oven
gilly_jenkin [afraid]: Dani! Somebody keep my little maid from the door, do not let her look in here!
-> rescue

~ rescue
if flag.n3_clock >= 7
Narrator: The bricks shimmer like summer tar, and the iron links biting Gilly's wrists have begun to glow a dull cherry red.
endif
* [Athletics DC 20] Wrench a chain apart -> chain_ok | chain_fail
* [Sleight of Hand DC 20] Pick a chain's lock -> chain_ok | chain_fail
* [Investigation DC 20] Find a weak link -> chain_ok | chain_fail
* [Arcana DC 20] Unpick the spell on a chain -> chain_ok | chain_fail
* [if flag.n3_slices < 3] Carve a slice of the roast -> carve
* [if not flag.stonoga_struck] Strike Stonoga -> stonoga_hit
* Talk to Gilly -> gilly_talk
* Step back for a moment -> END

~ chain_ok
Narrator: With a sharp crack, one of the heavy iron chains gives way and drops clanking into the ash.
set n3_chains += 1
-> tick

~ chain_fail
Narrator: The soot-slick iron rattles and burns your fingers, holding fast around her bruised arms.
-> tick

~ carve
Narrator: {name} slices a smoking strip from the turning bird; it tastes of sage and sweet orchard apples, cooling the burn in your lungs.
heal 2d8
set n3_slices += 1
-> tick

~ stonoga_hit
nm_stonoga [angry]: Ruin the gravy, would you? Let it burn, then!
Narrator: Your blow goes through her paper chef's hat like smoke, and she vanishes in a loud clatter of copper pans.
vanish nm_stonoga
set stonoga_struck
-> rescue

~ gilly_talk
gilly_jenkin [afraid]: Never mind me, just swear you will look after Dani and my Walter! Leave this hearth and get back to the porch.
gilly_jenkin [angry]: That child sees clear through the floorboards of the world, and the things she knows by heart frighten even her own mother.
-> rescue

~ tick
set n3_clock += 1
if flag.n3_chains >= 3
-> freed
elif flag.n3_clock >= 10
-> lost
else
-> burst
endif

~ burst
Narrator: The coals shift with a hollow roar, sending a sheet of yellow flame rolling across the bricks.
check Dexterity DC 17 -> burst_dodged | burst_hit

~ burst_dodged
Narrator: You duck behind the iron spit as the wave of heat washes harmlessly overhead.
-> rescue

~ burst_hit
Narrator: The fire catches your cloak and licks high around the spit, stealing precious breath from Gilly.
damage 2d10 fire
set n3_clock += 1
if flag.n3_clock >= 10
-> lost
endif
-> rescue

~ freed
gilly_jenkin [smile]: Oh, bless your hands, it is letting go!
Narrator: As the third chain falls away, a cool blue mist curls around Gilly's shoulders, smelling of rain on porch boards, and draws her gently up out of the heat.
cutscene nm_pulled_out
Narrator: A hand of blue mist closes round a hand, and the captive is drawn up and out of the dream.
cutscene nm_pulled_out_2
Narrator: Far away on the porch, Dani keeps her eyes shut, and a thread of blue light runs from her hands into the house.
cutscene end
vanish gilly_jenkin
set gilly_saved
set nm_oven_done
-> doorway

~ lost
Narrator: A ribbon of pale blue mist reaches down through the smoke, brushing Gilly's cheek like a child's hand before the roaring curtain of gold closes softly over her. When the glare parts, the iron spit hangs empty and still.
set gilly_dead
set nm_oven_done
-> doorway

~ doorway
Narrator: The banked coals settle to a hush, and in the back wall of the brickwork a crooked red door begins to glow.
-> END

~ door
if not flag.nm_oven_done
Narrator: Somewhere behind the wall of fire a door is waiting, but you cannot reach it through the blaze.
-> END
endif
Narrator: The crooked door stands among the cooling ashes, its brass handle warm to the touch.
* Step through -> toll
* [Performance DC 12] Tell the oven a joke -> joke_ok | joke_fail
* Not yet -> END

~ joke_ok
Narrator: A deep, grating chuckle rumbles up from the ash pit, and the angry coals settle into a gentle, rosy hearth-glow.
set dream_laughed
-> toll

~ joke_fail
Narrator: The bricks give a dry pop, wholly unamused by your wit.
-> toll

~ toll
if flag.dream_laughed
Narrator: Still warm with mirth, the oven lets you pass without taking a single blister for its fee.
set dream_laughed = false
-> pass
else
Narrator: As you reach for the latch, the brickwork draws one last greedy breath of heat.
check Constitution DC 17 -> pass | toll_hurt
endif

~ toll_hurt
Narrator: The iron latch sears your palm, taking its due in skin and cinder before it turns.
damage 1d10 fire
-> pass

~ pass
quest crooked_nightmare smoking_crater
move nm_crater
